   $q$How does the episode in which Imani skips three days help develop the theme?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It reveals that the gauge had been broken for most of the month of August.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Because nothing seems to happen, it shows why her effort feels pointless, which sets up the discovery that it counted.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows that Aunt Ruth secretly wants Imani to quit the volunteer job.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It proves that the network never actually used any of the readings it collected.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because nothing seems to happen, it shows why her effort feels pointless, which sets up the discovery that it counted.$q$, $q$No one notices the missing days, which makes Imani's doubt believable and gives the October letter its force. The letter shows the readings were used, so the network did not ignore them.$q$, 'draft', '92c764c7-3bff-5062-a5e9-22529b0ba6d9')
