   $q$Based on the first paragraph, why does Mateo most likely shorten his father's answer at first?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He wants his father to sound impressive, so he trims the personal details.","is_correct":true},{"text":"His father asked him beforehand to keep every answer as short as possible.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"He does not understand enough Spanish to follow his father's long answer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Ms. Halvorsen has told him that she only has time for very brief answers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He wants his father to sound impressive, so he trims the personal details.$q$, $q$The first paragraph says Mateo took pride in making his father sound like someone who belonged in any room, which explains why he cuts the personal story. His father later asks for every word, so he never requested short answers.$q$, 'draft', '449bc0cf-0735-56ec-90ec-03e29a31c04d')
