  ('9c8255dc-b0d0-5d8b-8f40-ea1049603a9b', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-theme-summary'), null, 'medium',
   $q$How does the kite's comparison of itself to the clouds at the beginning set up the theme?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that the kite is grateful to the girl for keeping it close to the hillside meadow.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It explains that the string was tied poorly and was always going to break on its own.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It proves that the kite can fly higher than the clouds whenever the afternoon wind is strong.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It establishes the kite's belief that freedom means having nothing attached, the belief the fable then tests.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It establishes the kite's belief that freedom means having nothing attached, the belief the fable then tests.$q$, $q$The kite envies the clouds because "nothing pulls at them," which sets up the mistaken idea the fall corrects. The kite complains about the girl's string, so it is not grateful at the start.$q$, 'draft', '22ab2113-ca53-5255-9921-de940cc475f3')
