   $q$Which choice is the best objective summary of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The speaker finds an old map and decides to dig up the creek so the town can see it again.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-false-detail"},{"text":"The speaker angrily blames the town for carelessly destroying its own beautiful history.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"The speaker learns from an archivist that Alder Creek was covered with stone in 1931.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Studying an old town map, the speaker finds a buried creek and vanished places, then listens for the creek on the walk home.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Studying an old town map, the speaker finds a buried creek and vanished places, then listens for the creek on the walk home.$q$, $q$The correct summary covers the map, the discoveries, and the listening walk home without adding feelings the poem lacks. The archivist detail is accurate but covers only one stanza.$q$, 'draft', 'f34a3c20-71b8-55e0-971c-23ba0630eb73')
